.TH GPU-SWITCHER 1 "31 October 2026" "gpu-switcher 0.1.0" "User Manual"
.SH NAME
gpu-switcher \- switch the primary display adapter (GNOME/Mutter)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gpu-switcher
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gpu-switcher
is a small GTK 4 GUI application for dual-GPU machines. It selects which
GPU the GNOME compositor (Mutter) uses as the
.BR primary
display adapter by managing the udev rule
.BR /etc/udev/rules.d/61-mutter-primary-gpu.rules
under polkit authorization, and activates the change via reboot or logout.
.PP
Only GNOME/Wayland sessions are supported in v1; in any other session the
app shows a warning banner and makes no changes.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/udev/rules.d/61-mutter-primary-gpu.rules
Managed udev rule. The app keeps
.BI .bak.
backups of previous rule contents.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR udevadm (8),
.BR lspci (8)
